WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.793
So you want to be a teaching artist?

2
00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:02.961
That's awesome.

3
00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:04.421
A teaching artist is basically

4
00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:06.673
just a practicing artist
who teaches.

5
00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:09.217
The trick is that a lot of people in society

6
00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:10.593
think you can just throw
an artist

7
00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:13.304
in the classroom, and they can just kinda teach.

8
00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:16.057
Artists are amazing, artists can do anything.

9
00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:17.726
But having some training and skills

10
00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:20.603
like classroom management, lesson planning,

11
00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:21.521
things like that,

12
00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.106
can really go a long way

13
00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:25.108
in terms of successful experiences

14
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:26.860
for you and your future students.

15
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.945
There are a lot of training
programs out there,

16
00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:31.781
some of which are associated
with non-profits

17
00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:33.950
who then hire teaching artists

18
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.910
and will then place you in schools,

19
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.829
museums, community centers.

20
00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:39.789
It might be one-off workshops

21
00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:41.791
or longer-term residencies

22
00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:43.668
in the classroom,
after school.

23
00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:44.961
The sky is really the limit

24
00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:46.713
in terms of what teaching artists can do.

25
00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.131
It's very helpful

26
00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.966
to have some arts
integration training

27
00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:51.217
so that you can connect the arts

28
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.886
with other academic subjects,

29
00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.345
and it's really helpful

30
00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:56.473
to have social emotional
learning training

31
00:00:56.473 --> 00:00:57.849
so that your arts teaching

32
00:00:57.849 --> 00:00:59.726
can enrich the whole person.

33
00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.186
It's also important to remember

34
00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:02.353
that being a teaching artist

35
00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:05.023
is often freelance gig work.

36
00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:07.358
You might even start
your own little business,

37
00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:09.277
and even if you don't,
you still really need

38
00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:11.946
to market your services
and to know what sets

39
00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:13.281
your teaching artistry apart

40
00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:14.949
because it becomes the product.

41
00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:16.910
I love being a teaching artist

42
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.912
because it's very independent,

43
00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:20.288
very dynamic.

44
00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:22.957
You can go from project
to project, do multiple jobs

45
00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:25.043
at the same time, take breaks

46
00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:26.586
to focus on your own artwork.

47
00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.754
But you have to know

48
00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.672
that's the lifestyle
you're signing up for.

49
00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:31.132
If this sounds like you,

50
00:01:31.132 --> 00:01:32.509
check out some of the training programs

51
00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.177
so that you can get started

52
00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:36.554
acquiring the tools and skills that you’ll need

53
00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:39.349
to enter the exciting world of teaching artistry.
